+#### Pruning finished branches and worktrees
+
+Finished branches and worktrees are pruned for you, so they do not pile up after every merged pull request.
+
+```bash
+ta cleanup --only branches --dry-run   # Show every branch, what cleanup would do and why. Changes nothing.
+ta cleanup --only branches             # Delete the safe ones, ask about the rest
+ta cleanup --explain branch:feature/x  # Full evidence for one branch
+```
+
+The pull request state comes from your VCS adapter, not from `git branch -d` or `git cherry`, because a squash merge rewrites commits and makes a finished branch look unmerged. A local branch is deleted without asking only when:
+
+- its pull request is merged and the branch has no commits beyond the head that was submitted, or
+- every commit on it is already in the default branch.
+
+Everything else is kept or put to you as a question, with the reason shown:
+
+| Situation | What happens |
+|-----------|--------------|
+| Pull request still open | Kept (shown as `skip`). |
+| Merged, but the branch has newer commits than the PR head | Asked. |
+| Pull request closed without merging, or no pull request at all | Asked. |
+| Worktree has uncommitted or untracked files | Asked, with the file list. The only offered answer is to keep it. |
+| Current branch, default branch (`main`, `master`, or what `origin/HEAD` names) | Never touched. |
+| Pull request state could not be read (offline, `gh` not signed in) | Kept, with the cause shown. |
+
+When a finished branch is checked out in a linked worktree and that worktree is clean, the worktree is removed first and then the branch. A worktree is never force-removed.
+
+Every deletion is recorded with the branch name and the commit it pointed at, in `.ta/cleanup/branches.jsonl` and in `.ta/audit.jsonl`. To get a branch back:
+
+```bash
+git branch feature/x 3f2a9c1d4e...   # the "recover" command is stored with each entry
+```
+
+Remote branches are never deleted by cleanup (GitHub deletes them when the pull request merges). A remote branch whose pull request was closed unmerged is listed as a finding, with the `git push origin --delete` command you can run yourself.
+
+Pruning runs on its own:
+
+- right after `ta draft watch` (or `ta draft apply --watch`) sees the pull request merged, and
+- in the daemon's periodic cleanup, even when `auto = "off"`.
+
+To turn it off, set `branches = false` under `[cleanup]` in `.ta/workflow.toml`.
+
